# Copy this file to .env.local (gitignored via *.local) for local dev.
# For the deployed build, set these as GitHub Actions repo secrets instead
# (Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions) — see .github/workflows/deploy.yml.
#
# Setup steps (Google Cloud Console — console.cloud.google.com):
# 1. Create a project (or reuse one).
# 2. APIs & Services > Enabled APIs > enable "Google Drive API".
# 3. APIs & Services > OAuth consent screen:
#    - User type: External.
#    - Publishing status: keep it in "Testing" (do NOT publish).
#    - Test users: add every Google account you want to allow in here.
#      This is what actually enforces "only these accounts" — Google itself
#      refuses the consent screen for any other account while in Testing
#      status. Any email not added here AND in VITE_ALLOWED_EMAIL below is
#      rejected twice over.
#    - The requested scope (see src/lib/auth/google-identity.ts) is full
#      Drive access, needed so more than one account can share the same
#      sync folder — appdata-only access is private per-account and can't
#      be shared. Because of this, the consent screen shows an "unverified
#      app" warning; click "Advanced > Go to [app] (unsafe)" to continue.
#      This is expected for a personal Testing-status app, not an error.
# 4. APIs & Services > Credentials > Create Credentials > OAuth client ID:
#    - Application type: Web application.
#    - Authorized JavaScript origins:
#        http://localhost:5173
#        https://flameheater.github.io
#    - No redirect URI needed (this app uses the token/implicit flow, not
#      the redirect-based auth code flow).
# 5. Copy the generated Client ID into VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID below.
# 6. If more than one Google account should share the same data: in ONE of
#    the accounts' Google Drive, create a folder (e.g. "KipLog Sync"), then
#    right-click it > Share > add every OTHER allowed account's email with
#    Editor access. Open the folder and copy its ID from the URL —
#    drive.google.com/drive/folders/<THIS PART> — into VITE_SYNC_FOLDER_ID
#    below. If only one account will ever use this app, still create a
#    folder for it (a private one is fine) so there's somewhere to sync to.

VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# One email, or several separated by commas (each must ALSO be a test user above):
VITE_ALLOWED_EMAIL=
VITE_SYNC_FOLDER_ID=
